  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Direct oral-bioavailability records for structurally related piperazine/CNS molecules are at or above the F≥20% threshold: eltoprazine complete/about 95%/102±29%/110±32%/95±16%, CAB near-complete, imipramine-N-oxide 100%, SB-742457 76–100% in rats (one 24% outlier), and bexagliflozin 78%.",
      "card_ids": ["C02","C03","C06","C14","C15","C17","C20","C21","C22","C29","C32","C33","C38","C47","C49","C53"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 absorption evidence for cilostazol, which shares the query's 3,4-dihydroquinolin-2(1H)-one and O-butyl linker, shows high Caco-2 permeability and high fraction absorbed in rats (0.953–0.995 at 0.5–1 mg/kg; over 95% overall; 88% in a separate rat study despite P-gp efflux), with L5 confirming high upper-intestinal permeability (Papp >1.92×10−5 cm/s) and regional absorption.",
      "card_ids": ["C119","C132","C145","C124","C110","C108","C149","C179","C166","C200","C173"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Cilostazol's very low aqueous solubility (~3 µg/mL) does not translate into low fraction absorbed in the same records, so the query's unfavorable solubility prior is not affirmative evidence for F<20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C117","C130","C135","C132","C145","C124","C110","C108","C149"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 efflux records for related motifs (2,3-dichlorophenyl piperazine PG01037 ER 4.3; dihydroquinolinone compound 1a ER 5) indicate possible P-gp involvement, but efflux alone is not affirmative evidence for F<20% and cilostazol retains high absorption despite P-gp efflux.",
      "card_ids": ["C191","C181","C149"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic-clearance records show CYP3A-mediated metabolism for related arylpiperazine/dihydroquinolinone molecules (NGB 2904, PG01037, cilostazol, ziprasidone) with moderate intrinsic clearance in some cases, but no direct F or matched oral/IV for the query; this is mechanistic first-pass context, not threshold-relevant low evidence.",
      "card_ids": ["C205","C207","C232","C212","C237","C240","C224","C222","C208","C250"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "contradictory",
      "decision_effect": "weakened",
      "card_ids": ["C205","C207","C232","C212","C237","C240","C224","C222","C208","C250"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule itself; all F evidence is from reference contexts.",
    "No matched oral-versus-IV AUC comparison for the query or a close analog; L6 records report clearance or metabolism without absolute F.",
    "Closest scaffold analog cilostazol differs in terminal group (tetrazole cyclohexyl vs 2,3-dichlorophenyl piperazine), so metabolic and efflux behavior may differ.",
    "No experimental solubility or permeability data for the query; high logD and partial ionization remain a dissolution concern.",
    "L6 hepatic-clearance records are for related but not identical molecules; query CYP3A/P-gp substrate status is not directly measured.",
    "No dose or formulation context for the query; oral bioavailability can be dose- and formulation-dependent."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "High: direct F records for related piperazine/CNS molecules and high absorption evidence for the shared dihydroquinolinone/butoxy scaffold support F≥20%; L6 hepatic-clearance records indicate possible CYP3A-mediated first-pass liability but no threshold-relevant low F evidence, so high prediction is retained with moderate confidence."
}

